  "title": "Higher-order thoughts are seldom conscious",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "f14ac55a-b149-4478-9dfe-6b8dc97d7648",
      "text": "A higher-order thought is conscious only if a third-order thought is about it, which seldom happens. So the theory predicts that people are seldom aware of the higher-order thoughts that make their states conscious, which matches experience, and no regress arises.",
